<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, oil, meal down.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, oil, meal down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>A bearish trend continued in Indian soybean prices on Tuesday, dealers said. Prices fell by 200-300 rupees per tonne in central Indian markets. Demand from processing plants was very poor. Business was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices fell by 300 rupees per tonne on increased selling from plants and refineries. Business volume was very dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices remained bearish. Soymeal yellow prices have fallen by $12-13 per tonne and was quoted at $255-257 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) at ports on the west Indian coast for export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction prices fell by $1 and quoted at $98-99 per tonne FAS (free alongside ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was 3,450-3,500 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition. Business volume was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
